  <title id="bdl04australiancredit-title">Empirical variance of posterior mean estimates against the number of processors on Australian Credit</title>
  <desc id="bdl04australiancredit-desc">Log-log plot of variance, from 0.000001 to 1, against the total number of particles MR from about 2,000 to 520,000, with the number of processors R from 4 to 1024 on the top axis and M equal to 511. All methods decrease roughly in proportion to the reference line R to the power minus 1. MH, PCN parallel and MH parallel are highest, falling from about 0.1 to 0.17 at R equal to 4 to about 0.0005 to 0.0007 at R equal to 1024. AIS and MH smMALA lie in the middle, from about 0.004 to 0.008 down to about 0.00002. SMC parallel pCN, RB-MP-MCMC and ARB-MP-MCMC are lowest and close together, from about 0.0008 to 0.0009 down to about 0.000002 to 0.000003.</desc>
